@startuml
title StopwatchBloc (Refactored) - State Diagram

[*] --> StopwatchInitial : app start / reset

StopwatchInitial --> StopwatchRunning : StopwatchStart
StopwatchRunning --> StopwatchPaused : StopwatchPause
StopwatchRunning --> StopwatchInitial : StopwatchStop
StopwatchPaused --> StopwatchRunning : StopwatchStart
StopwatchPaused --> StopwatchInitial : StopwatchStop

StopwatchRunning --> StopwatchRunning : StopwatchLapsUpdated (StopwatchRecordLap use case)
StopwatchPaused --> StopwatchPaused : StopwatchLapsUpdated (can't trigger StopwatchRecordLap but reacting to late updates is allowed)

note top of StopwatchRunning
  - State contains laps: List<LapEntity>
  - StopwatchService runs and emits msStream & lapStream
  - Lap updates handled via StopwatchLapsUpdated event
  - StopwatchRecordLap triggers usecase only; state update comes from lapStream
end note

note top of StopwatchPaused
  - State contains laps: List<LapEntity>
  - Stopwatch paused; msStream continues in service, 
    UI doesn't update elapsed time
  - Lap updates still handled via StopwatchLapsUpdated event
end note

@enduml
